# Special-right single-select filters

- Applies only to filters whose config has `condition: "dstleitung"` or `condition: "Personengruppe"`.
- Presence is rights-driven: special-right filters are removed first, then re-added only when the user has the matching filter right.
- If the user has no matching filter right, the filter must remain absent. Do not leave a visible wrapper that only looks disabled.
- The `Alle` option is controlled only by the `Alle` right, not by the per-filter right.
- Do not wait for tab traversal in special-right startup under `KDB3/js/dashboard/filters/`. Scope discovery must come from Cognos scope APIs such as `getAllScopeIds()` (via `core/cognosApi/` wrappers per `cognosAPI.mdc`), not from `_KDB.state.tabs.allTraversed`.
- Do NOT block early filter setup on a slow `Alle` table when the per-filter right is already known.
- Start the first pass as soon as the first relevant filter right (`dstleitung` or `Personengruppe`) is known. Do not block that first pass on the other filter-right table.
- Remove all special-right filters from all scopes first, confirm they are absent, then process whichever filter-right conditions are already known.
- Process later filter-right conditions incrementally when they resolve. Do not treat "unknown yet" as the same thing as `false`.
- Automatic special-right startup/default selection is global-only. Recreate allowed page-context tab filters too, but do not auto-write the global startup selection into those scopes.
- After rights are known, use a short `Alle` grace period (about 500 ms) to decide whether the first desired selection is config default or `Alle`.
- If filter right = true and `Alle` right = false:
  - keep the filter present
  - hide or disable the `Alle` option
  - force the configured default selection from filter config (`displayValue` + `useValue`)
- If filter right = true and `Alle` right = true:
  - keep the filter present
  - allow the `Alle` option
  - initialize the filter to `Alle` / empty values
- If `Alle` is still unresolved after the grace period, treat it as provisional `false` and apply the restrictive config default immediately.
- If `Alle` resolves to `true` later, run a second reconcile pass:
  - show `Alle`
  - replace the global Cognos filter context with `[]`
  - mirror the confirmed single-select state back to `Alle` in global scope
- The late `Alle` reconcile must be idempotent. Do not re-run it when the first pass already used `Alle`.
- Allowed filters must be recreated directly with the known desired values. Do not create an empty filter first and only later try to default it.
- A special-right filter is only confirmed present after Cognos reports the expected values for the global filter scope and a present filter API for relevant page-context scopes.
- The forced default or `Alle` value must be written only to global Cognos filter context and mirrored into `_KDB.state.filters.singleSelect.byScope.global` only after that confirmation step.
- Page-context filters may be restored for presence/availability, but they must not automatically inherit the global startup selection.
- Removal remains cross-scope so stale page-context copies are cleared first, while startup default selection remains global-only.
- The single-select feature owns popup behavior; special-right logic owns availability, forced defaults, and `Alle` permission.

See also: `cognosAPI.mdc`, `state.mdc`, `architecture.mdc` (update `filesExplained.md` / `eventSubscribe.md` when filter flows change).
